NAMING DECISION 2026-05-12 (Mark, interactive): pkix-profiles-cabf aliases mirror Profile struct slug, matching the existing web_pki_policy() / smime_policy() / code_signing_policy() convention. Final signatures:

```rust
// in pkix-profiles
pub fn check_basic_tls_shape(cert: &Certificate, now_unix: u64) -> Result<(), Vec<Finding>>;
pub fn check_basic_smime_shape(cert: &Certificate, now_unix: u64) -> Result<(), Vec<Finding>>;

// in pkix-profiles-cabf (revised from bead's check_cabf_*_shape proposal)
pub fn check_web_pki_shape(cert: &Certificate, now_unix: u64) -> Result<(), Vec<Finding>>;
pub fn check_smime_shape(cert: &Certificate, now_unix: u64) -> Result<(), Vec<Finding>>;
pub fn check_code_signing_shape(cert: &Certificate, now_unix: u64) -> Result<(), Vec<Finding>>;
```

Crate name (`pkix_profiles_cabf::`) already conveys CA/B Forum namespace; no need to repeat it in function names. Symmetric across pkix-profiles and pkix-profiles-cabf: each crate's shape-check aliases mirror its Profile struct slugs (BasicTlsProfile -> check_basic_tls_shape, WebPkiProfile -> check_web_pki_shape).

ALL HUMAN-DECISION-GATES NOW SETTLED:
- Dep-graph option (i) -- add pkix-lint as workspace dep of pkix-profiles + pkix-profiles-cabf -- approved 2026-05-11 (Mark, interactive).
- Naming option (2) -- mirror Profile struct slug -- approved 2026-05-12 (Mark, interactive).

REMAINING WORK is pure implementation: impl LintProfile on each Profile type, ship the five convenience aliases, write tests. Human label can be stripped.

PREREQUISITE BLOCKED ON: pkix-lint currently ships only Rfc5280MaxSerialLengthLint. BasicTlsProfile::lints() and BasicSmimeProfile::lints() would return effectively-empty Vecs. The shape-check aliases would be no-ops or near-no-ops without additional RFC-conformance lints. Filing a sub-bead for the missing lints (RFC 6125 SAN parts, serverAuth-EKU presence, RFC 8551 emailProtection-EKU presence, etc.) as a prerequisite to making this bead's shape-checks substantive.
